@misc{agda-F15-notinscope-repair-guessed-provider,
  section  = {cycle detection},
  claim    = {The ban-decompose NotInScope repair appended GUESSED provider imports, and every one of the 20 back-edges cut in this arc was one. The signature is uniform: a stripped using/renaming clause leaves a name unbound, and the repair appends the correct Foundation.Eq import AND a second, wrong module at the end of the import block — often a module that IMPORTS the file being repaired, i.e. exactly backwards. Witnesses: Substrate.Algebra.Module gained 'open import Substrate.Algebra.Q.Properties.AddMonoid' (a rationals-properties module pulled into the base Module record) creating a 34-module SCC. Substrate.Category.ConjugationCoalgebra gained 'open import Substrate.Groups.V4-Cosets' to supply lsuc, which V4-Cosets does not define, creating a 38-module SCC. The repair has no acyclicity check and no provider verification.},
