@misc{agda-B10-seed-map-dies-on-commit,
  section  = {finding},
  claim    = {scope_fix --seed recovers the name-to-owner map from the barrel at HEAD, and committing the uncommitted Coxeter severance destroys it},
  check    = {standing},
  note     = {kind=finding by=main. Witness INVERTED on purpose: it asks for a leaf that exists on disk but not at HEAD, so it refuses while the map is recoverable and flips OPEN when the split lands. Roughly 50 of the 166 NONEXPORT rows depend on that map. Ordering enforced by nothing. ⚑⚑ RETIRED-FALSE 2026-08-25 by the filer, re-derived independently before retiring. THE CLAIM ABOVE IS KEPT VERBATIM because the REASONING FAILURE is the transferable part. WHAT IS WRONG: scope_fix --seed reads RE-EXPORTS, not DEFINITIONS. seed_map (scratch/scope_fix.py, --source seed_map) runs 'git show HEAD:<path>' and then matches exactly three shapes -- 'public using (..)', 'using (..) public', and bare 'open import M public'. I observed that 'git show HEAD:Base.agda' returns the intact pre-split barrel carrying Gen, power and sigma-OrderOf, and concluded --seed could recover the map. That step is invalid: the barrel DEFINES those names, it does not RE-EXPORT them, and only re-exports are seeded. RE-DERIVED THREE WAYS, all reproducing: 'scope_fix.py --dry-run --seed Substrate/Groups/Coxeter/Cyclic/Base.agda' prints 'seed. 0 name(s)'; 'agda_defs --at HEAD Substrate.Groups.Coxeter.Cyclic.Base' shows a plain definition module with NO 'open import ... public' line at all; 'agda_defs --reexports' on it reports '0 site(s) in 0 of 3598 module(s)'. The zero is HONEST, not the empty-regex defect seed_map's own comment warns about -- that warning is about public and using COMMUTING, and both orders are matched. AND THE HAZARD IS INVERTED: the map lives in the UNTRACKED leaf files plus Base.agda's TRACKED working-tree body, which already opens all 13 leaves by name. A commit PRESERVES that map. 'git stash' or 'git clean' DESTROYS it. Anyone who acted on this entry protected against the wrong operation. SUPERSEDED BY agda-B11-seed-map-was-never-in-the-barrel, which measured it first and carries the positive account of where the map does live. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): RETIRED-FALSE 2026-08-25 — THE CLAIM BELOW IS REFUTED AND IS KEPT VERBATIM AS RESIDUE, because the REASONING FAILURE is the transferable part. ⚑ WHAT IS WRONG: scope_fix --seed reads RE-EXPORTS, not DEFINITIONS. seed_map (scratch/scope_fix.py — read it with pycodemod --source seed_map) runs git show HEAD on the path and then matches exactly three shapes: public using (..), using (..) public, and a bare open import M public. The filer observed that git show HEAD on Base.agda returns the intact pre-split barrel DEFINING Gen, power and sigma-OrderOf, and concluded --seed could recover the map. That step is invalid — the barrel DEFINES those names, it does not RE-EXPORT them, and only re-exports are ever seeded. ⚑ RE-DERIVED THREE WAYS 2026-08-25 by the filer, all reproducing: scope_fix.py --dry-run --seed Substrate/Groups/Coxeter/Cyclic/Base.agda prints seed. 0 name(s); agda_defs --at HEAD Substrate.Groups.Coxeter.Cyclic.Base shows a plain definition module with NO open import ... public line at all; agda_defs --reexports on it reports 0 site(s) in 0 of 3598 module(s). The zero is HONEST, not the empty-regex defect seed_map own comment warns about — that warning is about public and using COMMUTING, and both orders are matched. ⚑⚑ AND THE HAZARD IS INVERTED: the map lives in the UNTRACKED leaf files plus Base.agda TRACKED working-tree body, which already opens all 13 leaves by name. A commit PRESERVES that map. git stash or git clean DESTROYS it — anyone who acted on this entry guarded the wrong operation. ⚑ WHY THE KIND CHANGED FROM refuses: TO standing, and this is the load-bearing half: the old witness ran git show HEAD on .../Base/Gen.agda as a deliberate INVERTED COUNTDOWN, refusing while the leaf was absent from HEAD and flipping to exit 0 = OPEN the instant the split landed. Under the refuted mechanism that command tracks NOTHING — and worse, it is not merely inert: on the next commit of the split it would flip to OPEN and assert that the false hazard had ARRIVED. A witness that would come true about a refuted claim is worse than none. unwitnessed was rejected too, because unwitnessed means a witness is OWED and an honest gap remains; nothing is owed here, the claim is measured false. standing is the kind for a measured fact no code change can flip, and the fact now recorded is the REFUTATION. SUPERSEDED BY agda-B11-seed-map-was-never-in-the-barrel, which measured this first and carries the positive account of where the map does live. ⚑ THE ORIGINAL CLAIM, VERBATIM, FOLLOWS — DO NOT ACT ON IT: Ⓑ10 ORDERING HAZARD, and it is live and time-sensitive. scope_fix --seed recovers the name-to-owner map FROM THE BARREL FILE AT HEAD — seed_map's docstring: name to owning module, from the public re-export. The Coxeter.Cyclic.Base severance is UNCOMMITTED: Base.agda is MM and 13 leaves under Base/ are untracked, plus Bridge, Inverse, NthPower/Concat and InvCanonical/InvInv are MD with untracked replacements, 40-plus files total. MEASURED 2026-08-25: git show HEAD on Base.agda returns the intact pre-split barrel carrying Gen, gen-eq, power, Canonical-at, canonical-cover, sigma-HasOrderPerm and sigma-OrderOf. So the recovery map for roughly 50 of the 166 NONEXPORT rows EXISTS TODAY and is DESTROYED THE MOMENT that decomposition is committed. THE WITNESS IS INVERTED DELIBERATELY: it asks for a leaf path that does not exist at HEAD, so it FAILS while the barrel is still intact and recoverable, and flips to OPEN exit 0 the instant the split lands in HEAD. That is the correct direction — this finding is a countdown, not a standing fact, and a witness that passed after the map died would be worse than none. NOT VERIFIED BY COMMIT: I did not commit the split to observe the flip.}
}

@misc{agda-B10-clause-audit-blind-to-blind-spots,
