  note     = {kind=finding by=main. Measured on the first complete run, 166 NONEXPORT, ZERO blind spots. TraceDivides indexes 0 names from a mutual block and compiles clean, but nobody imports it with a clause so it cannot appear. Also: provides returning 0 is ambiguous between blind spot and stripped barrel, and only reading the file disambiguates. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): Ⓑ10 A GREEN NONEXPORT IS A FACT ABOUT WHICH MODULES ARE NAMED IN CLAUSES. check_clause_audit consults def_index only for the TARGET of an import clause, so a module whose definitions the index cannot see produces a NONEXPORT row ONLY IF some consumer names it in a using/renaming/hiding clause. MEASURED 2026-08-25 on the first complete run in this repo history, 6345 clause names, 166 NONEXPORT: ZERO were index blind spots. Algebra.Nat.GCD.TraceDivides genuinely indexes as 0 names because its definitions sit in a mutual block at line 30, and it COMPILES CLEAN — but it appears nowhere in the 166, because nobody imports it with a clause. So the gate is structurally incapable of surfacing the blind-spot class that def_index own comments record. ⚑ AND A RELATED AMBIGUITY THAT COST A DISPATCH ITS PREMISE: provides X returning 0 names is ambiguous between a genuine index blind spot and a legitimately-empty barrel whose public re-exports were stripped. In all 166 it was the barrel. The disambiguator is READING THE FILE, never the count — count-is-a-query-fact. UNWITNESSED because the discriminating quantity is a census VALUE over two populations and every behavioural kind here reads an EXIT CODE.}
