@misc{agda-B15-single-chokepoint-masks-all,
  section  = {finding},
  claim    = {One ClashingDefinition at Coxeter/Word.agda:38 masks the entire NONEXPORT population -- three unrelated probe modules abort there, none reaching a NotInScope},
  check    = {refuses:/home/mikemol/github/substrate/scripts/membudget,run,384,chokeprobe,--,agda,--safe,-i/home/mikemol/github/substrate/agda,/home/mikemol/github/substrate/agda/Substrate/Groups/Subgroup.agda},
  note     = {kind=finding by=agda-oracle axis=b. Ⓑ15 QUESTIONS 1 AND 3 ANSWERED TOGETHER, AND THE ANSWERS POINT OPPOSITE WAYS. A targeted typecheck is CHEAP -- measured via scripts/membudget run 384, agda --safe on the working tree: Groups/Subgroup.agda 0.35s CPU, Lojban/Fragment/Example1MiNelciDo.agda 0.24s, Cardinality/Product.agda comparable, Algebra/Semiring/Instances/Z.agda 0.46s. Against a ~56min-CPU full make that is roughly four orders of magnitude cheaper per site. BUT CHEAPNESS IS NOT THE CONSTRAINT. All three failing probes aborted at the IDENTICAL error in a file none of them names -- Substrate/Groups/Coxeter/Word.agda:38 ClashingDefinition, Multiple definitions of _++_, previous definition at Substrate/Foundation/List.agda:30. Agda halts scope checking at the first error, so NOT ONE of the NONEXPORT rows in those modules ever surfaced. The masking hypothesis is CONFIRMED and is worse than feared -- it is not many scattered maskers but ONE choke point standing in front of a large share of the population, reached transitively from both Groups and Lojban. ⚑ THE COROLLARY IS THE ACTIONABLE PART. Because it is a SINGLE edge, clearing that one ClashingDefinition is the highest-leverage move available, and it may unmask most of the population in one step. Rank with split_pipeline --leverage before assuming. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): Ⓑ15 A TARGETED TYPECHECK IS CHEAP (0.35s CPU) BUT ONE CLASHING DEFINITION MASKS THE WHOLE NONEXPORT POPULATION. Three structurally unrelated modules carrying NONEXPORT rows (Groups/Subgroup.agda, Lojban/Fragment/Example1MiNelciDo.agda, Cardinality/Product.agda) each aborted at the IDENTICAL third-party error: Coxeter/Word.agda:38 ClashingDefinition _++_ vs Foundation/List.agda:30. Agda scope-checking halts at the first error, so no NotInScope from any of the three ever surfaced. This is the masking hypothesis CONFIRMED: in a red tree the error you get is not the error that names the site you need. Cost per probe 0.11-0.31s user; a full make is ~56min CPU, so targeted probing is ~4 orders cheaper AND the cheapness is not the constraint -- the choke point is.}
}

