XPORT name I resolved still exists at a live leaf under its ORIGINAL SPELLING: agda_defs s-for -> SemidirectProduct.S; Stab -> SemidirectProduct.Stab; factorisation -> SemidirectProduct.Factorisation; v-of-axis -> Axes.VOfAxis; _+ℤ_ -> Algebra.Z.Add; _*ℤ_ -> Algebra.Z.Mul; Gen/insert/gen-≟ -> Coxeter.Cyclic.Base.{Gen,Insert,GenDec}. Nothing was RENAMED; the barrel's was stripped by Ⓑ1a so the name no longer transits. Reading the barrels confirms it (the disambiguator is the FILE, not the 0-count): SemidirectProduct.agda has 13 open imports and not one ; Coxeter/Cyclic/Base.agda likewise 13; Z/Arithmetic.agda says so in a comment at line 29 ('the three re-exports are STRIPPED (the ban)'). The repair is REBIND AT THE LEAF (scope_fix --seed / rewire_stale_module), NOT a rename. A rename here would rename a name that is not duplicated and is not misspelled.}
