  claim    = {A Bash-only subagent cannot create a file, because the no-chaining hook refuses heredoc, -c and printf redirection while --body-file needs a file it cannot make.},
  check    = {standing},
  note     = {kind=finding by=agda-oracle via substrate. Witness registered in findings.py, kind standing. ⚑ MEASURED TWICE THIS SESSION on the parent side: a transcript-miner dispatched to WRITE a directives file had its heredoc refused and had to return the content in its final message for the parent to write, and a second dispatch hit the same wall. So the constraint is not agda-specific — it binds every Bash-only agent this repo dispatches. ⚑⚑ The workaround this ledger uses is a one-line --body, which bounds what a subagent can file to what fits one argument. That is why an owed finding from a subagent arrives as prose in a report rather than as a filing, and why the parent must file it. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): heredoc, -c and printf > are refused by the no-chaining hook, and --body-file needs a file the agent cannot create; one-line --body is the workaround this ledger uses}
}

